{"id":"56a294856d8f96ddf5c98eb1079e072d7d368fb1","axis":"silent","repo":"phan/phan","sha":"56a294856d8f96ddf5c98eb1079e072d7d368fb1","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"NEWS.md","lines":["@@ -41,6 +41,15 @@ Performance improvements:"," - Cache the hash of an AST node (`ASTHasher::hash()`) in a `WeakMap` instead of a dynamic property of the node. PHP allocates a property table of 376 bytes for the first dynamic property of an object, and the hash was the only dynamic property of most of the nodes that had one: in Phan's analysis of itself, 27 % of the nodes of an analyzed file had a dynamic property, and 5 % do now. The saving in peak memory is small (2 MB of 724 MB for that run), because few of those nodes are alive at the same time. A modified clone of a hashed node no longer keeps the hash of the original node ([#5638](https://github.com/phan/phan/issues/5638))"," "," Bug fixes:","+- Fix crashes, a hang and internal exceptions found by running Phan on the test suites of php-src, Psalm and PHPStan. Phan now analyzes the following without crashing (it does not yet report all of them as errors):","+  - circular inheritance such as `class A extends B {}` with `class B extends A {}` (infinite recursion)","+  - `\\static` as a return type, `parent&Iterator` in a trait, `@return X&static` called on an intersection type, `self&B` in the phpdoc of a class constant, `value-of<T>` iterated with `foreach`, and `@extends`, `@implements` or `@use` with a type that is not a class (e.g. `class-string<T>`)","+  - `#[Attr(...)]` and `#[Attr(?)]` (now `PhanInvalidNode`), `class A extends parent {}`, `class A implements parent {}`, `@return parent` outside of a class and `parent::f()` outside of a class (now `PhanContextNotObject`)","+  - a `(void)` cast in a `for` loop expression, a `match` statement with a literal subject, `Foo::{$name}` as the default value of a parameter in an issue message, and the enum default of an internal function's parameter (e.g. `round()`) in an issue message","+  - constant folding that emits PHP notices or throws (`0 ** -1`, `$x |= 1.5`, `list(1.5 => $x) = ...`, `[PHP_INT_MAX => 1, 2]`)","+  - named arguments that skip a parameter of an internal function that a plugin analyzes (e.g. `sort(flags: SORT_STRING)`, `implode(array: $a)`, `in_array($x, strict: true)`, `array_filter($a, mode: ARRAY_FILTER_USE_KEY)`)","+  - a `match` arm in a loop with `redundant_condition_detection`","+  - a closure after a deprecated cast such as `(double)` (PHP 8.5+): the deprecation was emitted while parsing, which corrupted the line numbers of the closures that followed"," - Fix false positive `PhanPluginCaseMismatchNamespace` of `CaseMismatchPlugin` for a class name with a namespace that is not fully qualified, such as `DOM\\Node` for the class `\\Demo\\DOM\\Node` in the namespace `Demo`: the plugin compared it with the class `\\DOM\\Node` of the global namespace, which is `\\Dom\\Node` in PHP 8.4+. A casing mismatch in such a name is now reported against the class that the name refers to ([#5648](https://github.com/phan/phan/issues/5648))"," - Fix false positive `PhanTypeMismatchReturnReal` and other issues caused by an outdated type of a static property after calling a method that assigns it with `self::`, `static::` or `parent::`, when Phan does not know the type that the method assigns: in `if (self::$prop === null) { self::setProp(new stdClass()); } return self::$prop;`, the type of `self::$prop` stayed `null` when `setProp()` was declared after the calling method (it is analyzed later), inherited from a parent class, or declared in a subclass of the class that declares the property. The property now has its previous type or its declared type after such a call, or an unknown type if it declares none ([#5651](https://github.com/phan/phan/issues/5651))"," - Fix false positive `PhanIncompatibleCompositionConstant` for a trait constant with the same name as a parent class constant when the parent constant is private, when the class using the trait declares the constant itself, or when `minimum_target_php_version` is 8.5 or newer (from PHP 8.5 on, a trait constant overrides a parent class constant). `PhanIncompatibleCompositionConstant` is now also reported when the constants with the same name of two traits, of a class and a trait it uses, or (before PHP 8.5) of a parent class and a trait differ in `final` or in their declared type (only one of them has a type, or the types are not equivalent), which PHP rejects even when their visibility and value are the same. Types that are spelled differently but are equivalent, such as `?int` and `int|null`, are compatible, and types that contain `self` are not compared. `PhanConstantTypeMismatchInheritance` now also checks public constants imported from traits, and, for `target_php_version` 8.3 or newer, reports an untyped constant that overrides a typed constant of a parent class or an interface, which PHP 8.3+ rejects. This is not reported for a constant of an internal class when `target_php_version` is older than 8.4: Phan knows the type of such a constant from the PHP version running it or from its stubs, and most internal constants got their type in PHP 8.4. Issues about a trait constant that overrides an inherited constant (`PhanConstantAccessSignatureMismatch`, `PhanAccessOverridesFinalConstant`, `PhanConstantTypeMismatchInheritance`) are reported at the class using the trait. `self` in the type of a constant of a trait is the class using the trait in the subclasses of that class too: overriding such a constant below an intermediate subclass with the type of that class was a false positive `PhanConstantTypeMismatchInheritance`. A constant that a class imports from a trait now takes precedence over a constant with the same name of an interface that the class implements, as in PHP: Phan used the constant of the interface for such a class, and did not check the constant of the trait against it (its type, `final` and its visibility) ([#5647](https://github.com/phan/phan/issues/5647))"],"additions":9,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"internal/Issue-Types-Caught-by-Phan.md","lines":["@@ -569,6 +569,8 @@ Currently unused."," Saw a parse notice: {DETAILS}"," ```"," ","+e.g. [this issue](https://github.com/phan/phan/tree/v6/tests/php85_files/expected/5963_cast_crashes.php.expected#L1) is emitted when analyzing [this PHP file](https://github.com/phan/phan/tree/v6/tests/php85_files/src/5963_cast_crashes.php#L8).","+"," ## PhanCompatibleTraitConstant"," "," ```"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Phan/AST/ASTReverter.php","lines":["@@ -195,7 +195,12 @@ public static function init(): void","                 return implode(', ', array_map([self::class, 'toShortString'], $node->children));","             },","             ast\\AST_CLASS_CONST => static function (Node $node): string {","-                return self::toShortString($node->children['class']) . '::' . $node->children['const'];","+                $const = $node->children['const'];","+                if ($const instanceof Node) {","+                    // Dynamic class constant fetch (PHP 8.3+), e.g. `Foo::{$name}`","+                    return self::toShortString($node->children['class']) . '::{' . self::toShortString($const) . '}';","+                }","+                return self::toShortString($node->children['class']) . '::' . $const;","             },","             ast\\AST_CLASS_NAME => static function (Node $node): string {","                 return self::toShortString($node->children['class']) . '::class';"],"additions":6,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Phan/AST/Parser.php","lines":["@@ -133,28 +133,38 @@ private static function parseCodeHandlingDeprecation(CodeBase $code_base, Contex","         // and those errors might mess up language servers, etc. if ever printed to stdout","         $original_error_reporting = error_reporting();","         error_reporting($original_error_reporting & ~\\E_COMPILE_WARNING);",